# The runtime's bigs hold to their meaning (runtime/Big), on every case a
# property draws and every input of its boxes: each operation is what GMP's
# arithmetic states it is, the laws hold among the operations, each entry's
# small path gives what its large path gives, and every operation borrows
# its operands and returns one owned result (bigs.cpp). Each run draws its
# cases from a fresh seed, which a failure names; each check then runs
# again with its own planted fault, mostly a word operation's mistake at
# the small range's edges, and must catch it. The report beside the
# transcript says how the cases fell into classes.
. "$IDRIS_MLIR_ROOT/harness/testutils.sh"
. "$root/harness/prop/prop.sh"
prop_build "$here/bigs.cpp" "$work/bigs" || exit 0
# Debt: 20000 cases a property ran in under a second on the coding machine
# (the host's clang, arm64 macOS); the owner's build sets the number so
# that the program ends well within step_limit on both targets.
prop_run "$work/bigs" --cases 20000
